bug_descriptions |bug_id, line_num, content|
    web_render_fractional_layout_followups_2026-11-28, 0, "1. Text on a line holding a vertical-align top / bottom box is 2 device rows high at k=4: 'ab <svg height=41 style=vertical-align:top>' Chrome paints ab on rows 23..70 of the line, Simple 21..68 (align_inline_line_device_dy returns 0 for has_valign; Chrome keeps the device baseline 70)."
    web_render_fractional_layout_followups_2026-11-28, 1, "2. An inline-block height:12.5px below the strut paints 13 rows at k=1: Chrome 5..16, Simple 4..16. The block return rounds the half px up; a box hanging from the whole-px baseline snaps its top. The svg path has the rule (hangs_from_baseline), the block return does not."
    web_render_fractional_layout_followups_2026-11-28, 2, "3. A clear block whose top margin is larger than the float is placed by its margin: float 30.75px, clear:both margin-top:40.5px as first in-flow child of a 50px block: Chrome puts it at the float's bottom (device row 1323 of a block at 1200), Simple at 1362."
    web_render_fractional_layout_followups_2026-11-28, 3, "4. Partly covered svg edge px are not blended: width=50 viewBox='0 0 3 1' at k=4, Chrome blends row 789 (about 0.63 coverage) and columns 89 / 288, Simple leaves them unpainted. A whole-px svg still rounds its viewBox edges (min-height:17px on the same svg: Chrome rows 483..548, Simple 482..549)."
    web_render_fractional_layout_followups_2026-11-28, 4, "5. <br clear> and a float inside an open line keep whole-px float edges (not measured against Chrome)."
    web_render_fractional_layout_followups_2026-11-28, 5, "6. width:40.5px max-width:40px on an svg after text starts one px right at k=1: Chrome columns 22..61, Simple 23..62 (the box takes the px of a fraction the clamp removed)."
    web_render_fractional_layout_followups_2026-11-28, 6, "7. Text inside a vertical-align:middle inline-block is 1 device row high at k=4 (2 rows before the middle fix; the box itself is on Chrome's rows)."

bugs_active |id, severity, status, title, file, line, reproducible_by, created_at, updated_at, valid|
    web_render_fractional_layout_followups_2026-11-28, P3, fix-implemented-verification-pending, "web render: fractional layout follow-ups measured by the float / svg lane (7 gaps)", src/lib/gc_async_mut/gpu/browser_engine/simple_web_html_layout_renderer_layout_engine.spl, 2150, "see description lines; each has a one-line fixture and Chrome 159 rows", 2026-11-28, 2026-11-28, true

bug_investigation_logs |bug_id, line_num, content|
    web_render_fractional_layout_followups_2026-11-28, 0, "2026-11-28 frac-float-svg lane: all seven measured on work/webrender-frac-float-svg-20261128 against Chrome 159; 1, 2, 3, 5 and 6 are unchanged from base 8b2da8a67a1, 4 and 7 are what is left after the svg / middle fix. None fixed here."
    web_render_fractional_layout_followups_2026-11-28, 1, "2026-11-28 css-comment-frac lane (work/webrender-css-comment-frac-20261128, base 2bc96bcf7de): all 7 re-measured against Chrome 159 at k=1 and k=4 with one probe per side (decode_png_to_argb on Chrome's screenshot, the same queries on the engine2d cpu_simd frame). Items 1, 2, 6, 7: already match at base (stale shard numbers from 8b2da8a67a1); pinned as controls. Item 3: a crash, not geometry - the clearance code read Style.contain_layout / contain_paint, which do not exist, so a page whose clear block is the first child of a box without top border/padding stopped with 'semantic: undefined field contain_layout'; now reads the contain attribute (node_contain_layout, contain_value_contains_paint) and the existing logic matches Chrome (k=4 123..162, k=1 31..40). Item 4: a whole-px svg whose viewBox puts a shape edge between CSS px now takes the coverage path (k=4 283..348 + eaaaea blends, k=1 71..85 + fa2bfa vs Chrome fa2afa); the edge blend also runs at k=1. Item 5: br clear=left|right|all|both mapped to clear (HTML UA sheet) and the cleared line takes the float's exact bottom (k=4 695..766, base with br style clear 692..763)."
    web_render_fractional_layout_followups_2026-11-28, 2, "Evidence: fractional_layout_followups_device_rows_chrome159_spec base 2/5 (items 3, 4, 5 red) -> lane 5/5. 1x catalog lane = base on every page (overview 0.16 html 0.26 css-layout 0.37 css-paint 0.35 forms-media 0.33 animation 0.32 evidence 0.08 tab-bar 0.02); interpreter dispatches html/css-layout/css-paint +0.00 % with byte-identical 1x frames."
    web_render_fractional_layout_followups_2026-11-28, 3, "Final gates at 145cb11a91c: 4 mandatory specs as base (simple_web_renderer_spec 121/123 on base and lane, same 2 offscreen-witness failures), matrix 77 mismatching (PASS), 1x and 4x catalogs identical to base (4x: overview 0.01 html 0.01 css-layout 0.02 css-paint 0.01 forms-media 0.05 animation 0.02 evidence 0.00 tab-bar 0.01). The clearance-crash fix also turns svg_fractional_size_interactions_chrome159_spec (base 0/9 -> 9/9) and float_fractional_height_clear_chrome159_spec (base 0/10 -> 10/10) green; 10 other float/svg/css neighbour specs unchanged. The older fractional_layout_followups_chrome159_spec (ba32f7509eb) stays 3/5 on base and lane: AC-1 reads a device-y-offset prop the text command never carries (Chrome and Simple ab ink both rows 23..70 at k=4), AC-3 pins the internal split 330 + 3/4 where the lane emits 331 - 1/4; both are device row 1323, which is Chrome's (clear box 1323..1342). Left unchanged for its owner, not loosened."
    web_render_fractional_layout_followups_2026-11-28, 4, "2026-11-28 review fix (same lane): the whole-px svg coverage gate is narrowed to fractional or (edge_frac and radius == 0 and opaque); the wide gate dropped the partly covered edge px of a rounded (rx) or translucent rect at k=1 (Chrome f744f7 / eba1eb at x=2 of rect x=3.4 in a 16 px 0 0 24 24 svg; k=4 fd11fd / ef87ef at x=9). Pinned as item 4 of fractional_layout_followups_device_rows_chrome159_spec: lane 6/6, wide gate 5/6. CSS contain: layout (and strict / content) now blocks margin collapse and clearance through the parent via Style.contain_layout; css_contain_layout_margin_chrome159_spec lane 2/2, before 0/2 (Chrome y a2 41, b2 141, d2 331, e 400, e2 420)."

